    "limit_reached": false,
    "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
    "seconds": 71,
    "summary": "The ad service was running with its high-CPU load problem pattern switched on for every request, and I've turned it off.\n\n**Root cause:** The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `adHighCpu` set to `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Every other load-inducing flag defaults to `off`, so this one was the outlier. With it on, the `ad` service burned CPU on every request. The `ad` logs showed \"High CPU-Load problempattern enabled\" on each call.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Set `adHighCpu` `defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, using `kubectl replace`.\n- Restarted `flagd` so its init container re-copied the config. The init-config logs now show `\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"`.\n- Restarted `ad` to pick up the new flag state.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running with no restarts.\n- The new `ad` pod logs zero \"High CPU-Load\" lines, and ad requests are still being served normally.\n\n**Caveat:** The ConfigMap comes from the Helm release `astronomy-shop`, so a `helm upgrade` would restore `\"on\"` unless the chart values are also changed. I could not check the chart values from this shell. The durable fix is to set the `adHighCpu` default to `off` in the Helm values or the chart's flagd config.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 12,
